1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:08,425
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,677
- ♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:21,354
[Trinity, in English]
With a jaw-breaking score of 92.7…

7
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:26,359
And still the reigning queens
of Royale Rumble!

8
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:29,654
[Velma, in English] I beg to disagree!

9
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,449
<i>There should be no animals</i>

10
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:36,578
<i>being harmed in the competition!</i>

11
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:37,829
Eh, what's this?

12
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:41,458
- [audience] Ohh!
- Whoa!

13
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:42,709
That's right!

14
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:45,086
What's the use of having talent
if it won't wake up ever again?

15
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:48,381
[Trinity] Because the rules were violated…

16
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:53,720
[in English] we declare that
Karayom Kweens is the winner!

17
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,972
[audience cheering]

18
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,141
[music continues]

19
00:00:58,224 --> 00:00:59,934
- [Atoy] Audrey?
- [audience cheering]

20
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,478
Huh?

21
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,104
[Red] <i>Wait. I'm going</i>
<i>to send you a picture. Okay?</i>

22
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:06,232
Watch him.
He might try to infiltrate Velora Bay.

23
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:09,277
[Trinity, in English] If he shows up,
he will be killed on the spot.

24
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,529
[Uno] <i>I can infiltrate that.</i>

25
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,782
[in English]
Just plug this into their computer.

26
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:16,034
[Mercado, in English] <i>This is very risky.</i>

27
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:20,038
[in English] <i>They must follow protocol,</i>
<i>even if they're civilians.</i>

28
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:21,498
[Atoy] <i>I'll take care of them, sir.</i>

29
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:23,541
[receptionist] Michael V., is that you?

30
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:24,542
Ah-- oh--

31
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,836
- [Karla] Ouch!
- Who's that? [gasps]

32
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,589
Son of a thread!

33
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:31,049
Karla, it's dangerous here!

34
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:33,593
- Eh, why are you allowed to come?
- You.

35
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:36,262
- [Atoy] <i>I'll guard you.</i>
- [Karla] <i>Me?</i>

36
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:38,765
- You! You're so stubborn, huh!
- We'll escape from here.

37
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:40,266
- Huh? Escape?
- [goon speaking indistinctly]

38
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,392
What will you do?

39
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:44,437
[Ibyang] <i>Brother, bother,</i>
<i>can I go to the bathroom?</i>

40
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,856
<i>I really need to pee.</i>

41
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,983
That's Rizaldo Coloma, right?

42
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:52,445
[Kurt] He's the corrupt mayor and the--
the bagman!

43
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:53,696
- [swishes]
- [groans]

44
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,532
[in English] Meet the princess of Amrati.

45
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:58,201
[Martina, in English] You know, my husband
would've loved to meet you too.

46
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,161
So, you're here too, you animal?

47
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:02,539
[Atoy] You even joined forces,
you two demons.

48
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:04,457
♪ <i>Like a bubble, like a bubble</i> ♪

49
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:05,458
♪ <i>When the cutter</i> ♪

50
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:07,210
[Samir, in English] Surprised to see me?

51
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,462
Turns out you wronged both me and Samir.

52
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,506
Where are my children?

53
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,842
PREVIOUSLY

54
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:16,553
[music fades]

55
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:22,767
[footsteps tapping]

56
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:25,562
Why are you still looking
for your children?

57
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,605
You won't see them again.

58
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,190
[somber music playing]

59
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:30,692
Now I'll finish you.

60
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,068
- [thumps]
- [grunts]

61
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:37,115
[ominous music playing]

62
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:43,121
You want to get back at me, don't you?

63
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,080
Revenge!

64
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:46,749
You're only brave because
you have many people with you.

65
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,212
You stay there. No one interfere, ah.

66
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:55,091
- [grunts]
- [thumps]

67
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,050
[tense music playing]

68
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:58,261
- [grunting & groaning]
- [thumping]

69
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:03,641
- [grunting & groaning]
- [thumping]

70
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:06,102
[theme music playing]

71
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:11,232
- [motorcycle revving]
- [sewing machine whirring]

72
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:14,193
- [scratches]
- [snipping]

73
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:18,072
[sewing machine clacking]

74
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,866
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

75
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:22,035
[thumps & gunshots]

76
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:26,289
- [music intensifies]
- [clicking]

77
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:31,502
[electronic blipping]

78
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,004
[music fades]

79
00:03:33,087 --> 00:03:35,506
[man] Bro, look at this.

80
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,176
Hmm. Looks normal.

81
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:40,011
But seems like there's something.

82
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:45,433
[suspicious music playing]

83
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:47,852
Hey. What are you doing here?

84
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,437
Bro.

85
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,397
[music continues]

86
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:52,982
Possible.

87
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:57,528
- [music fades]
- [rousing music playing]

88
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:59,155
[thumping and thudding]

89
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:03,910
- [growling, grunting, groaning]
- [rousing music playing]

90
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:15,505
[in English] Uhm, please excuse me.
I-- I have to go check on something.

91
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:16,422
Okay, okay.

92
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:23,179
[suspicious music playing]

93
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:29,060
[in English] Did you see the tall man
who was standing here a while ago?

94
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:30,687
Ah, uhm…

95
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:34,524
[in English] No, no tall man.

96
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:35,900
He was…

97
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:41,864
[security, in English]
Is there any problem, Mr. Ambassador?

98
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:45,910
[in English] I am looking for Atoy Padua.

99
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:48,329
I knew it was him!

100
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,124
He owes me plenty!

101
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,168
He will pay!

102
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,713
[security] How does he look like, sir?

103
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:59,299
[in English] He is a tall man
in a black suit.

104
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:03,011
Uhm, wait, wait. I have a picture.

105
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:06,973
Ah, there. This is him.

106
00:05:07,056 --> 00:05:11,352
[tense music playing]

107
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:15,356
He looks like the bodyguard
of the princess of Amrati.

108
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:19,402
- Princess of Amrati?
- Yes, sir.

109
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:20,903
Is she here?

110
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:23,823
She's-- supposed to be sick!

111
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:27,243
[music fades]

112
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:31,331
There! That's her!

113
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:35,209
[ominous music playing]

114
00:05:57,482 --> 00:06:02,361
[suspicious music playing]

115
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:06,991
[Martina, in English] This is…

116
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,035
Tonet and her brother.

117
00:06:10,536 --> 00:06:11,954
[What-- what the hell.

118
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:14,373
Is he here?

119
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,542
[Mongki] From Tabang Lupa.

120
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:18,711
How did he end up here?

121
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:20,797
Madame, maybe you're being haunted.

122
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,340
That's the one you killed
at the mall, right?

123
00:06:22,423 --> 00:06:23,716
[heavy music playing]

124
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,219
[in English] You know, you don't have to
remind me of that, Mongki, huh.

125
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:28,012
[Martina] Let's go.

126
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:30,389
You're ruining the night.

127
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:57,083
You animals.

128
00:06:58,042 --> 00:06:59,544
Especially you, Martina.

129
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:04,715
[music swells]

130
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:07,552
- [music fades]
- [tense music playing]

131
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:09,554
[grunting & groaning]

132
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,638
[thumping]

133
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:12,974
[thumping]

134
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:20,481
[grunting & groaning]

135
00:07:26,904 --> 00:07:32,201
[suspicious music playing]

136
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:40,209
[goon] Stay there! Eat there too!

137
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:44,589
- [music continues]
- [door closes]

138
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:52,513
- What?
- Why?

139
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:56,434
I'm hungry. And I even saved some for you.

140
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:58,394
I got salt and pepper too, eh.

141
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:01,939
That has sleeping pills in it.

142
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,734
Huh? Are you sure?

143
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:08,696
- Yes. Sleeping pills.
- Sleeping pills?

144
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:12,617
Oh, no. I already took a bite.

145
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:17,747
[ominous music playing]

146
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:20,416
Drink water. Lots of water, huh.

147
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,543
All of it? So it won't be too effective.

148
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:27,256
They want us to fall sleep,
so they can transfer us to the ship.

149
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:31,594
- [tense music playing]
- [gasps softly]

150
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:32,970
To the ship?

151
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,555
To the ship.

152
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:37,558
Huh? Where will they take us?

153
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,270
I don't know.

154
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,897
[music fades]

155
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,315
Eh, what about them?

156
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:46,067
[rousing music playing]

157
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:48,903
[Kalaf, in English] Thank you all
for coming to my birthday.

158
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:52,365
The drinks and food are plenty.

159
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:55,326
- [in English] Where's Atoy?
- [Karla] Huh?

160
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:57,954
He left. Why?

161
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,081
Someone saw him here.

162
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:03,209
We're dead. Let's go, let's leave.

163
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,586
Wait, wait. Don't you have a performance?

164
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:10,383
If we leave now, they'll notice, right?

165
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:12,885
Of course they'll look for you.

166
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:15,888
Let's just follow the plan.
Let's wait for Uno.

167
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:21,060
[suspicious music playing]

168
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:23,604
Karla, we need to go to them.

169
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:25,648
They need to know what's happening.

170
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:28,859
[Kalaf, in English] Ah, before we continue
with the party…

171
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:31,320
and with the other performers,

172
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:35,866
I would like to call
my, uhm, special guest.

173
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:38,828
The princess of Amrati.

174
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:44,000
Princess Priya Noorani! Where is she?

175
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:46,377
[tense music playing]

176
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:49,213
Thank you for coming to my party,
Princess Priya.

177
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:53,259
I'm glad you are feeling better.

178
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:56,095
[music swells]

179
00:09:56,178 --> 00:09:58,681
[in English] Of course, she is better.

180
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:02,351
[in English] She is not princess.

181
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,895
[intense music playing]

182
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,897
Sir Padua, I'm in.

183
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,567
- [panting]
- [soft rock music playing]

184
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:10,943
Where are you now?

185
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:17,533
[Mercado, in English] All you have to do
is plug this into their computer.

186
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:19,201
<i>Once you do that,</i>

187
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:23,331
<i>our IT team can access their system.</i>

188
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:28,169
- [computer blipping]
- [music swells]

189
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,212
Hey! Who are you?

190
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,673
[staff 1]
What are you doing here? Security!

191
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,675
- [action music playing]
- [grunts]

192
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:37,345
- [thudding]
- [groaning]

193
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:41,140
- [thumping]
- [grunting & groaning]

194
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:48,356
[computer blipping]

195
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:56,989
- [thumping]
- [grunting & groaning]

196
00:10:57,073 --> 00:11:01,452
- [grunting & groaning]
- [thumping]

197
00:11:01,535 --> 00:11:03,371
- [thumps]
- [grunts and groans]

198
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:06,248
Huh.

199
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,878
[thumps, then thuds]

200
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:15,049
- [grunts & groans]
- [music continues]

201
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:23,182
[grunts and groans]

202
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,148
[groaning]

203
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,537
[music fades]

204
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:47,248
Oh, my god!

205
00:11:47,331 --> 00:11:51,210
- [in English] You are an impostor!
- [Karla] No--

206
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:53,421
You are not princess!

207
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:55,673
[Kalaf, in English]
I don't believe this! Who are you?

208
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:57,925
[suspicious music playing]

209
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,802
Who are you?

210
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,973
You are with Atoy.

211
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:05,641
Where is he?

212
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,893
Uh, I don't know! Please, let me go!

213
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:10,354
[in English]
You are not going anywhere!

214
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:11,897
Help me!

215
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,149
- [gun cocks]
- [women squeal]

216
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,608
[shouts] Let her go!

217
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:19,989
- [gunshots]
- [screaming and panicking]

218
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:21,824
[chandelier shattering]

219
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:24,201
Let me go!

220
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,995
- Karla, let's go!
- Let me go!

221
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:27,246
- Let's go!
- Gavin?

222
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:28,247
- Let's go!
- Karla, come on!

223
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:31,417
[screaming and panicking]

224
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,127
[gunshot]

225
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,337
- [Kurt] Go. Go, go, go!
- Hide! Cover, cover, cover!

226
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,884
- [gun cocks]
- Get this.

227
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:41,969
We're ready, we're ready.

228
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:45,055
- [grunts and groans]
- [gunshots]

229
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:47,391
Brother Kurt,
Atoy didn't teach us that, ah.

230
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:50,060
[in English] I served in the marines.
And it's a secret!

231
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,020
We need to move! There are more of them.

232
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:53,022
[Kurt] Let's go!

233
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:58,068
[gunshots]

234
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,823
[music continues]

235
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,744
[computer blips]

236
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:12,082
[soft rock music playing]

237
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:17,922
Yes!

238
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:21,717
[in English] Sir Mercado,
the package is loaded.

239
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,595
Radar systems are disabled.

240
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,555
Security is breached.

241
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,140
[Mercado, in English] <i>We have control.</i>

242
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:33,062
<i>Rescue and back up operative</i>
<i>are now engaged to move to Velora Bay.</i>

243
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:34,313
Copy, sir.

244
00:13:34,813 --> 00:13:35,940
[grunts]

245
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:39,735
[music continues]

246
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:45,324
Where are my children?

247
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:49,870
[grunting]

248
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:52,665
[rock music playing]

249
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:54,124
[grunts]

250
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:57,253
[gunshots]

251
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,090
[gunshot and thumps]

252
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:06,262
[gunshots]

253
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:12,768
[tense music playing]

254
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,520
[Mongki] Martina!

255
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:16,939
Martina!

256
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:19,775
[tense music playing]

257
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:21,110
Martina.

258
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:23,362
Mongki, I've been looking for you.

259
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:24,446
[in English] What the hell is going on?

260
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,282
[panting] I spoke with Boss Red.

261
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:27,825
He said Atoy is here.

262
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,952
Looks like he's the one
shooting it out in there.

263
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:31,996
[in English] Oh, so what are we
supposed to do now?

264
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:32,955
Where is he?

265
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,373
He said he'll follow.

266
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,917
But he said you should go ahead
to the port.

267
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,502
We'll go back for Boss.

268
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,045
[in English] Okay, fine. Go!

269
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:42,006
- Go, go, go, go, go, now!
- Come on. Come on, come on.

270
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:48,554
[tense dramatic music]

271
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:55,895
- [slaps]
- [gasping]

272
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,147
[in English] How dare you!

273
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,900
How dare you your face! [gasping]

274
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,986
It was you-- you killed my sister.

275
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:06,864
[gasps]
You killed my sister. I'll kill you!

276
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,407
[Emerson gasps]

277
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:09,742
[music swells]

278
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:10,826
[grunts]

279
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,579
- I'll kill you!
- [grunts]

280
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:14,538
I'll kill you!

281
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:17,207
You killed my sister! [grunts]

282
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:20,127
[in English] Tonet is a nosy girl!
She deserved to die!

283
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:22,421
And there's nothing you can do about it!

284
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:23,923
- [Emerson] That's what you think!
- [groans]

285
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,299
Let me go.

286
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:26,508
- I'll kill you!
- Let me go.

287
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:27,801
- Let me go!
- You killed my sister!

288
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:29,053
- [groans]
- [grunts]

289
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,304
- Let me go.
- [Gavin] Brother Emerson, don't!

290
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,972
[Emerson grunting]

291
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,182
- [Gavin] Brother!
- [Emerson] Let me go!

292
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:36,393
Gavin! She killed Tonet! You killed Tonet!

293
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:38,562
You killed my sister!

294
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:40,481
[growls]

295
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:42,441
Hey! Go ahead! Try it!

296
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:43,734
What are you waiting for?

297
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:44,944
- [Mongki] Try it!
- Shoot her!

298
00:15:45,819 --> 00:15:46,737
Hurry!

299
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,322
- Martina, let's go!
- [grunting]

300
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:51,283
[tense music playing]

301
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,368
[grunts]

302
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,745
[in English] Gavin,
what are you doing here?

303
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:57,164
Helping fight the bad people.

304
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:59,875
- [gasping]
- Is it true you killed Tonet, huh?

305
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,335
- [Karla] Gavin, she--
- Is it true?

306
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:04,338
[in English] No matter what I've done,
I'm still your mother!

307
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:05,255
No!

308
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:06,840
- You should be on our side, Gavin!
- No, Mom!

309
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:08,384
- What are you saying?
- You need to pay for that!

310
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:10,135
[gasps] No. No, what are you saying?

311
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:11,762
Come home, come home!
Just come home with us, please.

312
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,263
Mom, no!

313
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:15,975
Stop this! Stop this, Gavin! Stop this!

314
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:17,393
Did you do it, Mom?

315
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,353
It doesn't matter!
You should be on my side!

316
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:21,438
[shouts] No! You need to pay for that!

317
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:23,524
[grunting]

318
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:25,859
[Martina] Why are you doing this?

319
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:27,611
- Mom…
- [thumps & gunshot]

320
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:29,029
Is it true?

321
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,739
- [Martina] Why are you doing this?
- It doesn't make sense!

322
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,577
[tense music playing]

323
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,662
- No!
- Mom, stop!

324
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:38,038
- Gavin, you need--
- Let go of that!

325
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:40,082
Get out of the way! Please, son! Please!

326
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:40,958
- Stop it! Get out of the way, son.
- Drop that!

327
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,376
- Mom!
- Get out of the way!

328
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:43,711
- I'm telling you--
- No!

329
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:45,254
- Let go, Mom!
- Get out of the way!

330
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:48,632
Gavin, please! Gavin, let go! Let go!

331
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:49,842
- Let go--
- [gunshot]

332
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:51,301
[gasps]

333
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,012
- Gavin?
- Oh, my god.

334
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,305
Gavin! Gavin, Gavin!

335
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:57,141
Oh, my god. I'm so sorry.

336
00:16:57,224 --> 00:16:58,392
I didn't mean it. I swear, Gavin. Please.

337
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:00,894
- Wake up, baby. Baby!
- [Karla] Gavin, Gavin!

338
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:01,895
I'm so sorry. Please!

339
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:04,440
- Gavin?
- [sobbing] No!

340
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:07,693
Look what you've done!
Gavin! My son, please wake up!

341
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:10,154
- Wake up, Gavin.
- Wake up, Gavin! Please!

342
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,364
- Please don't do this.
- Gavin.

343
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:13,741
- No one move!
- [gunshot]

344
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,159
- [Uno] No one move!
- [Martina] Wake up.

345
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:17,202
- [others] Hey. Hey, hey!
- [Uno] Stop!

346
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:18,912
[Uno] Gavin! What's happening to you?

347
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:19,830
- Gavin!
- Gavin.

348
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:21,915
Ah, hold Mommy!

349
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,250
- [Martina] What's happening?
- Hold Mommy!

350
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,461
- [shouts] What?
- What are you doing?

351
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:27,421
Surrender now with Mongki, Mom!

352
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,006
What are you doing? What are you doing?

353
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:30,924
There's someone here,
there's someone here! [gasps]

354
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:32,384
- [gunshots]
- Gavin!

355
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:33,635
- [gunshots]
- [screaming and panicking]

356
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,179
Martina! Martina! Let's go!

357
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:37,556
- Let me go!
- No! Wait!

358
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,558
[Nestor] Come on!
Come on, come on, come on! Come on!

359
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:41,435
[gunshots]

360
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:45,647
[ominous music playing]

361
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:49,985
[speaking in Russian] Say hi to God.

362
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:53,864
[gunshots]

363
00:17:57,117 --> 00:18:01,163
[intense music playing]

364
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,181
- Huh?
- Janine?

365
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,600
- Oh?
- Don't sleep.

366
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:25,145
- We still have a plan!
- I'm sleepy-- it's making me drowsy.

367
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:27,815
Then just slap me, okay. [grunts]

368
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:33,987
Just slap me.

369
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:35,823
[slaps]

370
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:41,286
No effect. Oh, no.

371
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,996
Or maybe…

372
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:47,376
[music continues]

373
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:53,006
Janine, I know how to wake you up.

374
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,801
- Bite the side of your nail.
- This one?

375
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:57,136
[Ibyang] Bite it.

376
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:00,389
Then pull the skin.

377
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:03,767
[gasps] Quick, quick! Hurry!

378
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,019
[clicks tongue, grunts]

379
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:08,438
Oh, there.

380
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:13,986
Ouch! [groans]

381
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,988
- What was that?
- [sneaky music playing]

382
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:19,032
[shushing]

383
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,122
- Sorry.
- [groans]

384
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,002
Okay. Lie down, lie down.

385
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:32,421
Close your eyes, but don't sleep, okay.

386
00:19:32,504 --> 00:19:34,256
I really won't be able to sleep.

387
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,799
It stings, eh.

388
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,514
Go, close your eyes.

389
00:19:45,475 --> 00:19:47,769
[music fades]

390
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:50,355
Take that one.

391
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,985
[suspicious music playing]

392
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:57,654
Boss, we'll load this onto the ship.

393
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,531
No, Atoy is there.
We'll take them somewhere else.

394
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:08,790
[phone rings]

395
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:11,919
Hello? Oh? Where are you?

396
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:13,420
[music fades]

397
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:16,089
[footsteps clomping]

398
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,384
No, no, no. Wait.

399
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:22,679
Go ahead. [grunts]

400
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:25,515
[ominous music playing]

401
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:26,892
Atoy is here.

402
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,269
I'm sure he's got company.

403
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:36,485
What?

404
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:38,570
Gavin is here?

405
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:53,335
Hello? Hello? What happened?

406
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:56,213
- [groans]
- [tense music playing]

407
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:57,256
- [goon] Boss!
- [groans]

408
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:00,133
[groans]

409
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:02,261
Janine, Janine! Hurry!

410
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:03,553
- Hurry, Janine!
- [groans]

411
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:06,014
- Go after them!
- Okay, Boss!

412
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:11,311
[Uno] Gavin! Hurry!

413
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:14,731
Wait. I need to find Martina.
She shouldn't be able escape.

414
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:17,943
Where's Atoy? Maybe he needs our help.

415
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:20,696
Okay. Let's find Atoy, and the children.

416
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:21,905
That's our priority.

417
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:22,823
Come on.

418
00:21:22,906 --> 00:21:25,575
Karla, stay here with Gavin.
Come on, come on!

419
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:27,327
I'm fine, just a graze!

420
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:29,621
[rousing music playing]

421
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:31,665
Let's go.

422
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:34,543
[suspicious music playing]

423
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:35,669
Come on.

424
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:37,796
Hurry.

425
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,761
Why did you stop? Come on!

426
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,596
They might catch us!

427
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:49,308
Go ahead. Go to your father.

428
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:53,395
Huh? We'll both go to Tatoy.

429
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:54,438
[Janine] No, no.

430
00:21:54,521 --> 00:21:56,315
They'll just catch us.

431
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:57,607
Just run.

432
00:21:58,191 --> 00:21:59,526
What about you?

433
00:22:00,235 --> 00:22:02,988
I'll create a distraction,
so they won't follow you.

434
00:22:10,787 --> 00:22:12,331
Come on! Here, this way!

435
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,542
Hey! Where are you going?

436
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:19,504
[tense music playing]

437
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:24,968
Where's the chopper?

438
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:28,764
[crickets chirping in the distance]

439
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:29,973
[dagger swishes]

440
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:34,686
- [dagger swooshes]
- [guttural cry of pain]

441
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:38,690
[tense music playing]

442
00:22:40,650 --> 00:22:42,402
You think you can escape, you corrupt man?

443
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:45,489
- [dagger swooshes]
- [guttural cry of pain]

444
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:47,699
You're a plague to Filipino taxpayers!

445
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:55,415
[Rizaldo] Ouch! [guttural cry of pain]

446
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:03,048
[Ibyang] Tatoy!

447
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:08,428
- [Ibyang] Let me go!
- [sobbing]

448
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:10,722
You're truly bad, you bald man!

449
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:15,852
[heavy music playing]

450
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:20,857
- Tatoy!
- [Atoy] Child?

451
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:26,404
- My child.
- [music swells]

452
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:35,914
Ibyang!

453
00:23:35,997 --> 00:23:41,795
- [electronic blipping]
- [intense music playing]

454
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,384
[officer, in English]
You are all under arrest!

455
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:50,804
[in English] I have diplomatic immunity!

456
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:52,597
- [Janine] Mommy.
- [theme music playing]

457
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:54,724
[in English] Thank God you're okay, child.

458
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,560
Janine, where is Ibyang?

459
00:23:57,144 --> 00:23:58,562
Let my child go.

460
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:00,772
Face me.

461
00:24:00,856 --> 00:24:02,607
You're really a skilled tracker,
Master Cutter.

462
00:24:02,691 --> 00:24:04,860
But you've cornered me now.

463
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:07,028
So, we all go down together.

464
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:08,697
Tatoy!

465
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:11,533
UP NEXT

466
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:13,535
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

467
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:14,870
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

468
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:17,455
<i>♪ Holding the scissors ♪</i>

469
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:20,542
<i>♪ One cut, and it's over ♪</i>

470
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,421
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
